          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The assumption that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong Weakly Initial Set of Covers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WISC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WISC
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+multiple+choice"} axiom of multiple choice
            and the axiom of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+violations+of+choice"} small violations of choice
            (which both imply it), it says intuitively that “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AC
            fails to hold only in a small way” (i.e. not in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper-class
            way).
          %h2#statement_for_sets Statement (for Sets)
          %p
            Precisely,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi WISC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WISC
            is the statement that for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi surj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set/X)_{surj}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/X
            consisting of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
            has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+initial+set"} weakly initial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↠
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\colon P_i \twoheadrightarrow X\}_{i\in I}
            such that for any surjection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ↠
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q\twoheadrightarrow X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
            which factors through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
          %h2#relationships_to_other_axioms Relationships to other axioms
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                WISC is implied by
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ↠
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\twoheadrightarrow X
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                is projective is necessarily a weakly initial (singleton) set in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi surj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set/X)_{surj}
            %li
              %p
                WISC is also implied by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+multiple+choice"} axiom of multiple choice
                (which is in turn implied by COSHEP). For if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is in some collection family
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi c
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi c
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{D_c\}_{c\in C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi c
                      %mo ↠
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_c \twoheadrightarrow X
                is weakly initial in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi surj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set/X)_{surj}
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%A0W-pretopos"} ΠW-pretopos
                satisfying WISC is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+topos"} predicative topos
            %li
              %p
                Since
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rathjen"} Michael Rathjen
                proves that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SVC"} SVC
                implies
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AMC"} AMC
                (at least in
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
            %li
              %p
                WISC also follows from the assertion that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+exact+completion"} free exact completion
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generic+proof"} generic proof
                (so that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{ex/lex}
                is a
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %li
              %p
                WISC implies that the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
                between any two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+category"} essentially small
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor#SizeQuestions"} here
            %li
              %p
                WISC implies (in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinals"} regular cardinals
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Karagila14"} Karagila
          %h3#applications Applications
          %h4#local_smallness_of_anafunctor_categories Local smallness of anafunctor categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              WISC implies the local essential smallness of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi ana
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_ana
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              be small categories and consider the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi ana
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{ana}(X,Y)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi j
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (j,f) : X \stackrel{j}{\leftarrow} X[U] \stackrel{f}{\to} Y
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[U] \to X
              is a surjective-on-objects,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
              functor. The underlying map on object sets is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X_0
              and a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to U
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi k
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X[V] &amp;  \to  &amp;  X[U]    \\
                    \&amp; k \searrow &amp; \downarrow j\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[V] \to X
              is the canonical fully faithful functor arising from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to X_0
              (the arrows of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[V]
              are given by
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                            %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^2 \times_{X_0^2} X_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j,f)
              to a span with left leg
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi ana
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{ana}(X,Y)
              is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of anafunctors where the left leg has as object component an element of the weakly initial set of surjections. Since there is only a set of functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[V] \to Y
              for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to X_0
          %h4#existence_of_higher_inductive_types Existence of higher inductive types
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Swan18"} Swan
            showed that WISC implies the existence of
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                W-types with reductions
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/W-types+with+reductions"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
          %h2#in_other_sites__external_version In other sites - external version
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            with a singleton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+pretopology"} Grothendieck pretopology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi cov
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C/a)_{cov}
            be the full subcategory of the slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/a
            consisting of the covers. WISC then states that
          %ul
            %li
              For all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi cov
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C/a)_{cov}
              has a weakly initial set.
          %p
            This definition is called
            %em external
            because it refers to an external category of sets. This is to be contrasted with the
            %em internal
            version of WISC, discussed below.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Assuming AC for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              with any of its usual pretopologies satisfies 'internal WISC'. Consider, for instance, the pretopology in which the covers are the maps admitting local sections, i.e. those
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon Y\to X
              such that for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              there exist an open set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\ni x
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(U)\to U
              is split epic. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              satisfies AC, then a weakly initial set in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi cov
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top/_{cov}X
              is given by the set of all maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒰
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{U\in \mathcal{U}} U \to X
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}\subset \mathcal{P}(X)
              is an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon Y\to X
              admits local sections, then for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              we can choose an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \ni x
              over which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              has a section, resulting in an open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U} = \{U_x \mid x\in X\}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒰
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{U\in \mathcal{U}} U \to X
              factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              merely satisfies WISC itself, then a more involved argument is required.)
          %p And now a non-example
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
              can be equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fpqc+topology"} fpqc topology
              (so this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fpqc+site"} fpqc site
              over
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{Z})
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Stacks0BBK"} Stacks Project Tag 0BBK
          %p
            More generally, for a non-singleton pretopology on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Given a site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            subcanonical, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            finitely complete, we can define a (weak) 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ana
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ana(C,J)
            of internal categories, anafunctors and transformations. If WISC holds for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,J)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ana
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ana(C,J)
            is locally essentially small.
          %h2#in_other_categories__internal_version In other categories - internal version
          %p
            To consider an
            %em internal
            version of WISC, which doesn’t refer to an external notion of set, one needs to assume that the ambient category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a strong enough
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack+semantics"} stack semantics
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#vdBM12"} van den Berg and Moerdijk
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+set+theory"} category of classes
          %p
            Importantly, the internal form of WISC is stable under many more categorical constructions than other forms of choice. For instance, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
            inherits WISC from its base topos of sets (even if the latter is constructive or even predicative); see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#vdBerg12"} van den Berg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SVC"} SVC
          %h2#References References
          %ul
            %li#vdBM12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Axiom of Multiple Choice and Models for Constructive Set Theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.4045"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Realizability Models for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CZF
                          %mo +
                          %mo ¬
                          %mi Pow
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CZF + \neg Pow
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/CIZF/rmczfnp.pdf"} unpublished note
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi TTCA
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TTCA_f
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TTCA
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TTCA
                stands for “type-theoretic collection axiom).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em WISC is independent from ZF
                %a{:href => "http://www.staff.science.uu.nl/~berg0002/papers/WISC.pdf"} PDF
            %li#vdBerg12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
                ,
                %em Predicative toposes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0959"}> arXiv:1207.0959
                ). In this paper WISC is called the “axiom of multiple choice”.
            %li#Swan18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Swan"}> Andrew Swan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em W-Types with Reductions and the Small Object Argument
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.07588"} arxiv:1802.07588
          %p The following two papers give models of set theory (without large cardinals) in which WISC fails.
          %ul#Karagila
            %li#Karagila14
              Asaf Karagila,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Embedding Orders Into Cardinals With
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi DC
                          %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DC_\kappa
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4064/fm226-2-4"} 10.4064/fm226-2-4
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.4396"} arXiv:1212.4396
          %ul
            %li#Roberts15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Michael+Roberts"}> David Michael Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The weak choice principle WISC may fail in the category of sets
              %a{:href => "http://link.springer.com/journal/11225"} Studia Logica
              Volume 103 (2015) Issue 5, pp 1005-1017, doi:
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s11225-015-9603-6"} 10.1007/s11225-015-9603-6
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3074"} arXiv:1311.3074
          %p The Stacks Project shows how to construct a counterexample to WISC from any set of fpqc covers of an affine scheme.
          %ul
            %li#Stacks0BBK
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BBK"} Tag 0BBK
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/foundational+axiom"} foundational axiom
